@startuml
title ChessFlow — Diagramme de classes métier

top to bottom direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #34536D
  FontColor #172B3A
  HeaderBackgroundColor #DCEAF5
}

class Player {
  - national_id: str
  - last_name: str
  - first_name: str
  - birth_date: date
  + validate_national_id()
  + to_dict()
  + from_dict(data)
}

class Tournament {
  - name: str
  - location: str
  - start_date: date
  - end_date: date
  - number_of_rounds: int = 4
  - description: str
  - participants: list[Player]
  - player_scores: dict[str, float]
  - rounds: list[Round]
  - status: str
  + add_participant(player)
  + can_start()
  + start_round()
  + update_scores()
  + is_finished()
  + to_dict()
  + from_dict(data)
}

class Round {
  - name: str
  - start_datetime: datetime
  - end_datetime: datetime | None
  - matches: list[Match]
  + add_match(match)
  + is_complete()
  + close()
  + to_dict()
  + from_dict(data)
}

class Match {
  - player_one: Player
  - player_two: Player
  - score_one: float | None
  - score_two: float | None
  + set_result(score_one, score_two)
  + has_result()
  + involves(player)
  + to_dict()
  + from_dict(data)
}

Tournament "0..*" o-- "2..* {even}" Player : participants
Tournament "1" *-- "0..*" Round : rounds
Round "1" *-- "1..*" Match : matches
Match "0..*" --> "1" Player : player_one
Match "0..*" --> "1" Player : player_two

note right of Player
  Le joueur existe indépendamment
  de tout tournoi. Son identifiant
  national est unique dans le registre.
end note

note right of Tournament
  Les scores sont propres au tournoi
  et indexés par l'identifiant national.
  Une ronde est créée progressivement.
end note

note bottom of Match
  Résultats autorisés :
  1–0, 0–1 ou 0,5–0,5.
end note

legend bottom left
  o--  agrégation : le joueur reste indépendant
  *--  composition : le cycle de vie dépend du parent
  -->  association vers un joueur
  Aucune classe abstraite ni relation d'héritage
endlegend
@enduml
